{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/69575-thoughts-on-changelings-stuck-in-the-hedge","id":69575,"title":"Thoughts on Changelings stuck in the Hedge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-10T19:52:54-08:00","id":69575,"title":"Thoughts on Changelings stuck in the Hedge?","content":"So, I forget which book it's in offhand, but I know in one of the sections that gives advice on the changeling's escape from Arcadia that it is possible to be so mutated that one could be locked out of reality, and is forever at best, stuck in the hedge. I've always thought this was a cool idea, and lately I've found myself with the chance to use one of these &quot;barred&quot; (I used to call them Exiles in my planning docs, but I think Barred works better as they're unable to enter the real world, rather than forced out of the real world), and I'm pondering if anyone else has used this kind of concept before in their games for NPCs or even PCs.<br /> <br /> First though, I may as well share my current thoughts. So far I figured that any NPC groups of these barred would need a hollow with special properties, as otherwise I'm betting they run a very high risk of being re-captured, killed, or turned into some kind of hobgoblin thing. Otherwise...mechanicly, i've been thinking of using select transmutations for the Pandorians and Centimani from Promethian to reflect their sheer...grotesqueness, and to give them something to set them apart from their less constricted fellows. The way I figure, the barred are close to becoming Hobgoblins once they run out of clarity (or Fae if their Wyrd is high enough), and maybe a possible hook for them is that they highly value anything from the real world to the point where it's one of the few ways they can possibly remain sane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T21:14:35-08:00","id":69606,"title":"","content":"There's the simple consideration of course, that any changeling who spends an extended time in the hedge (permanently in this case) starts to lose clarity dots quite quickly from a) Not having any human contacts to re-align their world views with 'normal' and b) Spending time in a realm that is for all things considered dreamlike and psychoactive. Any Changeling in this circumstance would be pretty short-lived as a changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T08:12:34-08:00","id":82637,"title":"","content":"I haven't used the mechanic as described, however I would suggest that having a Hollow should prevent the clarity loss, or at least slow the loss dramatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:49:40-08:00","id":84714,"title":"","content":"This is such an original thought, I wouldn't be surprised if you had a hard time finding anyone else with ideas down this rabbit hole. I'm fascinated by it's potential, though. My thoughts have been that if you get stuck in the Hedge, then you become part of the Hedge and forget most or all of what you were as a mortal (this is my version of clarity loss-- you forget yourself and most or all of the ways of mortality). <br /> <br /> I have a NPC who is a dryad and she has only a few flashes of memory from the mortal world-- she truly believes herself to be the Spirit of the Oak that she is bound to. I imagine that those bound in the Hedge are desperate for Glamour, unless they have a good source of Goblin Fruit for it. I would have creatures offer challenges of riddling and other contests in a bid to win some Glamour. <br /> <br /> I don't know if this might be useful, but I have a odd element in my Hedge-- they are Niggler Fish. They are only visible to people with low clarity and goblins and they float around and attach themselves to changeling's unguarded thoughts in the Hedge, then their feeding causes people to worry obsessively because they feel like they are forgetting something important (which is somewhat true as the fish nibble at memory). Goblins catch them and use them to store memories so they can sell them at the Market. So some clarity loss in the Hedge is due to the Hedge, but some of it is a result of Niggler fish infestation (which can be protected against if you know what to do). Also, you can regain some Clarity (or other things) from consuming a Niggler that has fed on the right thoughts....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:42:45-07:00","id":95621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GitariArt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/69575-thoughts-on-changelings-stuck-in-the-hedge?p=82637#post82637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't used the mechanic as described, however I would suggest that having a Hollow should prevent the clarity loss, or at least slow the loss dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would further suggest, that there is a small list of things that would keep your Clarity:<br /> <br /> * Motley member is with you (two points create direction, two Lost create relationship)<br /> * You have a Fae Mount, Hedge Beast, or some other relationship accessory<br /> * You are in/near a Hollow, if it is yours, no loss of Clarity is possible, if you are guesting in the Hollow, you need to be supported by mortal food and/or other mortal touchstones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}